Two caveats I am carrying forward rather than resolving. First, these are consolidated one-line summaries, not the experiments themselves; the compression may have dropped effect sizes, segment restrictions, and confidence intervals, so I treat their direction as more reliable than their magnitude. Second, a real downstream risk: stripping signup and onboarding fields removes the qualification data that feeds routing, and memory_44 says enterprise pipeline quality depends on the sales-assisted path. Optimizing self-serve completion could quietly degrade lead qualification and enterprise pipeline quality while the headline funnel metrics improve. Also, the current declines may be composition effects from the competitor pulling price-sensitive accounts out of the top of the funnel rather than genuine product friction, in which case a friction fix will underperform. I therefore run this as a standard experiment with holdout, guarded on retention and qualified-pipeline quality (not just completion and activation), with enterprise-routing fields preserved, and I will not read a completion-rate lift alone as success.","confidence":66}
